---
title: Spicy Red Lentil Koftas
yield: 12%skewers
course: Main
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
---

Soak #12 wooden skewers{12} in water for ~{30%minutes}. Put the @red lentils{175%g} in a #large pan{} and cover with cold water. Bring to the boil and cook for about ~{15%minutes} until tender but not mushy. Drain well.

Heat 4 tablespoons of the @vegetable oil{6%tbsp} in a #frying pan{}, add the coooked lentils, @green chilli{1}(deseeded and finely chopped) and @garlic clove{1}(crushed) and fry for 2 to ~{3%minutes} until softened slightly. Add the @spring onions{3}, @ground cumin{1%tbsp}, @ground coriander{1%tsp}, and seasoning and cook for ~{2%minutes}. Stir in the @gram (chickpea) flour{4%tbsp} and cook for a further 1 to ~{2%minutes}. Transfer the lentil mixture to a bowl and leave to cool. Add the @egg{1%small}(beaten) and stir the mixture thoroughly to bind. Chill for ~{1%hour}.

With wet hands, mould the lentil mixture on to the skewers to make 12 koftas, pressing firmly so that they do not fall apart during cooking. Brush the koftas with the remaining vegetable oil and grill for ~{10%minutes}, turning occasionally, until golden.